  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Siege Bound is a simple tower defense game where you have to defend your
    base against waves of monsters.


    You have access to 3 different types of
    towers that have different costs and accordingly have proportionate stats. Flying
    mobs can only be targeted by Archer and Mage towers.


    Mobs have various
    attributes such as different stats such as speed, health, as well as a reward
    for when they are slain. Each wave will progressively get harder to defend against.


    Camera
    movement is controlled by WASD, QE, Control and Space, as well as ZC. WASD control
    forward, backward, left, and right movements while Q and E control left and right
    rotation of the camera. Control and Space move the camera up while Z and C control
    the up and down pitch of the camera.


    Data is only saved when utilizing
    UI Buttons for level or menu switching.


    Best of luck in defending,

    Kevin
    Lin and Edmund Chin'
